body: "{\n  \"sprint\": \"8.2\",\n  \"title\": \"Formula-heavy block — 11 parsers via Code-First generator + WACC integration\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-05-24\",\n  \"status\": \"COMPLETE\",\n  \"composite_score\": 1.0,\n  \"deliverables\": {\n    \"code_first_generator\": {\n      \"file\": \"scripts/rail-ap-elite-50500-021563/W8/generate_sprint8_2_parsers.py\",\n      \"loc\": 380,\n      \"outputs\": 11,\n      \"templates\": 3\n    },\n    \"parsers_shipped\": [\n      {\"file\": \"wacc.rs\", \"sheet\": \"WACC\", \"layout\": \"SCATTER\", \"fields\": 13},\n      {\"file\": \"painel_controle.rs\", \"sheet\": \"Painel de Controle\", \"layout\": \"SCATTER\", \"fields\": 11},\n      {\"file\": \"demonstrativos_financeiros.rs\", \"sheet\": \"Demonstrativos financeiros\", \"layout\": \"TIMELINE_TRIPLE_HEADER\", \"fields\": 16},\n      {\"file\": \"balanco_patrimonial.rs\", \"sheet\": \"Balanço Patrimonial\", \"layout\": \"TIMELINE_CUSTOM(first_data_row=3)\", \"fields\": 13},\n      {\"file\": \"depreciacao_amortizacao.rs\", \"sheet\": \"Depreciação e amortização\", \"layout\": \"TIMELINE_STANDARD\", \"fields\": 6},\n      {\"file\": \"capex_capital.rs\", \"sheet\": \"CAPEX Capital\", \"layout\": \"TABULAR(header_row=2)\", \"fields\": 9},\n      {\"file\": \"capex_lcc_sustaining.rs\", \"sheet\": \"CAPEX LCC+Sustaining\", \"layout\": \"TABULAR(header_row=1)\", \"fields\": 5},\n      {\"file\": \"capex_frota.rs\", \"sheet\": \"CAPEX Frota\", \"layout\": \"TIMELINE_STANDARD\", \"fields\": 5},\n      {\"file\": \"opex_ambiental.rs\", \"sheet\": \"OPEX Ambiental\", \"layout\": \"TIMELINE_STANDARD\", \"fields\": 5},\n      {\"file\": \"leasing.rs\", \"sheet\": \"Leasing\", \"layout\": \"SCATTER\", \"fields\": 7},\n      {\"file\": \"fretes.rs\", \"sheet\": \"Fretes\", \"layout\": \"TABULAR_STANDARD\", \"fields\": 8}\n    ],\n    \"integration_tests\": [\n      {\"file\": \"sprint8_wacc_integration.rs\", \"invariants\": 5, \"pass\": 5, \"elapsed_secs\": 3.23, \"production_validated\": true}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"total_tests_pass\": 118,\n    \"lib_tests_pass\": 95,\n    \"integration_tests_pass\": 23,\n    \"parsers_total_shipped\": 16,\n    \"parsers_remaining_long_tail\": 11,\n    \"rl_rewards_this_sprint\": 3.0,\n    \"rl_rewards_taco_forge_perfect_edit\": 9.9,\n    \"compile_time_clean_secs\": 7.56\n  },\n  \"production_validated\": {\n    \"capex_3_corridors\": \"10/10 PASS in 4.05s\",\n    \"opex_3_corridors\": \"8/8 PASS in 3.27s\",\n    \"wacc_3_corridors\": \"5/5 PASS in 3.23s\",\n    \"regression_check\": \"zero — pre-existing tests unaffected by Sprint 8.2 additions\"\n  },\n  \"layout_classification_final\": {\n    \"TIMELINE_STANDARD\": [\"CAPEX\", \"OPEX\", \"Depreciação\", \"CAPEX Frota\", \"OPEX Ambiental\"],\n    \"TIMELINE_TRIPLE_HEADER\": [\"Receitas\", \"Demonstrativos financeiros\"],\n    \"TIMELINE_CUSTOM\": [\"Balanço Patrimonial (first_data_row=3)\"],\n    \"TABULAR_STANDARD\": [\"Demanda - OD\", \"Fretes\"],\n    \"TABULAR_CUSTOM\": [\"CAPEX Capital (header_row=2)\", \"CAPEX LCC+Sustaining (header_row=1)\"],\n    \"SCATTER\": [\"RESUMO\", \"WACC\", \"Painel de Controle\", \"Leasing\"]\n  },\n  \"lessons\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L42\",\n      \"title\": \"calamine::Range::from_sparse anchors at min(row,col), not (0,0)\",\n      \"context\": \"Test fixtures that put first Cell at (header_row, 0) cause Range to start at (header_row, 0), making get_size() return relative dims. Add Cell::new((0,0), Data::Empty) as the first cell to anchor the Range at (0,0). Production .xlsm reads always start at (0,0) so behavior is correct in real data — only test fixtures need the anchor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L43\",\n      \"title\": \"Code-First Python generator scales linearly for templated parsers\",\n      \"context\": \"Wrote 380 LOC generate_sprint8_2_parsers.py with PARSERS list spec + 3 templates (TIMELINE/SCATTER/TABULAR). Produced 11 staging .rs.txt files (4.0-4.6KB each = ~46KB total) in <1s. Compared to writing 11 individual Write calls (~46KB each), saved ~40KB of context. Template substitution via Python .format() suffices for Rust code with no dynamic types.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L44\",\n      \"title\": \"taco-forge perfect-edit batch via shell loop is the production canonical workflow\",\n      \"context\": \"for parser in $LIST; do taco-forge perfect-edit --path X --content-from Y; done shipped 11 parsers in ~5 seconds with full VGP + atomic + post-validate + memory + RL per file. REGRA #14 honored 11x in one sprint.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_sprint\": \"8.3 — 11 long-tail parsers (Capa, Característica_Trecho, Frota-INPUT LEASING, Gráficos, Tabelas, Auxiliares, input.demanda, Input-OPEX, Demais Linhas, Depreciação Aux, CAPEX e OPEX_Ambiental). Same 3 helpers + Python generator pattern. Then 8.4 PyO3 expansion + 8.5 cross-corridor diff + 8.6 Python thin wrapper + 8.7 E2E bench.\",\n  \"hash_chain_predecessor\": \"2026-05-24-sprint8-1-timeline-block-complete.toon\"\n}\n"
